.HE " " "The Australian UNIX Users Group" " "
.FO "Peter Ivanov"
.PA
We have so far achieved three half yearly meetings of the Australian
UNIX Users Group, two at the University of New South Wales, an a third
at the Australian Atomic Energy Commission.
The next meeting will be at the University of Sydney on September 1st, 1978.
Our host their will be Ian Jackson from the Basser Department
of Computer Science.
.PA
Some points on the agenda are:
.BP 7 3
*	Production of, and contributions to, a local newsletter.
.NP
*	Discussion of PWB UNIX, recently received at the Australian
Graduate School of Management.
.NP
*	The local user accounting system, and associated Cambridge SHARE
based sheduler (AUSAM) and experiences with its use during the first half
of 1978.
.NP
*	The continuing story of Wollongong University and their Interdata UNIX.
.NP
*	Anything else that takes our fancy.
.EP
.PA
As may be seen from the attached list of Australian users, UNIX
has come a long way in this country since the first level V system
was brought to life at UNSW.
.PA
However, we are far removed from the Anglo-American UNIX
mainstream, so should anybody find themselves stranded in Australia
I feel sure there are many people only too willing to make them feel at home.
